From 679e135d21573ad1e4f0a8e76b4b82c3f557417a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Rao <jack.rao@baseten.co>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:44:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] perf(rope): env-gated THD RoPE cu_seqlens host cache
 (BT_THD_ROPE_HOST_CACHE) [baseten]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MLA-style interleaving forces the unfused THD RoPE path:
_apply_rotary_pos_emb_thd issues ((cu_seqlens[1:] - cu_seqlens[:-1]) //
cp_size).tolist() plus per-sequence .item()s — blocking pageable
device-to-host copies, 2 per layer (q/k rope), 587 per step and 14.8s of
CPU at the 78-layer 2-microbatch 131k shape, replayed under full
recompute. (Site correction to the original attribution: the 15s memcpy
class is this RoPE bookkeeping, not sort_chunks_by_idxs — the TE fused
chunk_sort path is active.)

cu_seqlens is a per-microbatch constant shared by all layers: take one
host copy per unique tensor object (module-level FIFO cache, 64 entries,
strong refs so ids cannot recycle) and run all host reads on it. Each
entry also records the tensor's _version counter and hits only while it
matches — an in-place mutation of a cached cu_seqlens forces a fresh
copy instead of silently serving stale seqlens. Identical integer values
and arithmetic => bitwise exact; steady state has zero device syncs in
this function (624 -> ~4 blocking DtoH copies per step).

Env-gated, default OFF; gate off => byte-identical path. One-time
WARNING gate-state line per process.

Evidence (LPS-1062, 2026-08-09, golden EP16/CP16, 131k x 4 microbatches,
2x8 B300): together with the companion BT_DSA_CP_LAYOUT_CACHE,
634-645 -> ~715 tok/s/GPU steady (+11-13%); 16k x d32 customer shape
612 -> 726 (+18.5%). Loss canary drift <=2e-3, memory flat.
Parity: test_thd_rope_host_cache_parity.py — 167 PASS (CPU): gate
off/on bitwise through the real _apply_rotary_pos_emb_thd, both freqs
formats, both interleave modes; cache identity, _version mutation-miss,
and FIFO bound covered.
Records: experiment_artefacts/glm/lps_1062_perf/runs/
overnight_20260809_dispatcher_hostsync/ (REPORT.md, PATCH_NOTES.md).

PP2/CP8/EP8 @131k A/B on the 73c24b00 lineage (2026-08-13, LPS-1062
E2 spec section 3b): <TO FILL TONIGHT — d4 vs 918, d16 vs 1052
tok/s/GPU; canary band loss 12.2-12.4, grad-norm comparable>
